{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAPuxHD33xjuApy5X4hN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `watch::Receiver::mark_unchanged`. It makes the receiver treat the current value as already seen, so it's the opposite of `mark_changed`.\n\n**`tokio/src/sync/watch.rs`**: the method sits right after `mark_changed` and has a doc comment:\n```rust\npub fn mark_unchanged(&mut self) {\n    let current_version = self.shared.state.load().version();\n    self.version = current_version;\n}\n```\nAfter calling it, `has_changed()` returns `false` and `changed()` waits for the next send. The current value isn't borrowed, and the call doesn't fail if the sender has been dropped.\n\n**`tokio/tests/sync_watch.rs`**: the new `rx_mark_unchanged` test covers two cases:\n- It undoes an earlier `mark_changed()`, and `changed()` then waits.\n- It marks a newly sent value as seen, and `borrow_and_update()` still returns that new value.\n\nAll 10 tests in `sync_watch` pass. The 3 compiler warnings come from the `assert_ready_err!` macro, not from this change. I haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":686,"cache_read_input_tokens":33852,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":686,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"040325d3-49db-496a-b739-6903c27c1687","uuid":"66e33ada-297f-401c-a48d-a491f51e987e","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:15:47.381Z","request_id":"req_011CgAPux5JNkWC7AV36UWDW"}
