ter calling it, `has_changed()` returns `false` and `changed()` waits for the next send. The current value isn't borrowed, and the call doesn't fail if the sender has been dropped.\n\n**`tokio/tests/sync_watch.rs`**: the new `rx_mark_unchanged` test covers two cases:\n- It undoes an earlier `mark_changed()`, and `changed()` then waits.\n- It marks a newly sent value as seen, and `borrow_and_update()` still returns that new value.\n\nAll 10 tests in `sync_watch` pass. The 3 compiler warnings come from the `assert_ready_err!` macro, not from this change. I haven't committed anything.","ttft_ms":3094,"type":"result","duration_ms":41707,"uuid":"ceb9b245-c75b-4c86-b2d1-a884ec1e2ed7","ttft_stream_ms":1879,"time_to_request_ms":137,"first_content_frame_ms":1880,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
